cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to T32 in your work, please cite the specification as below."
title: "T32: A Compact Universal Timestamp"
abstract: >-
  T32 writes any moment as 8 base32 characters: a count of atomic (TAI)
  seconds since the start of 2000, offset so the past encodes too. A stamp's
  length is its resolution, every stamp names an interval, text order is time
  order, and a prefix is a range query.
type: software
version: "draft 0.2"
date-released: "2026-10-31"
authors:
